suggested_issue_body:
## Summary

The repository contains `FbxExporter` and `FbxImporter` (and `package.json` lists `fbx` as a keyword), but `Scene.save` and `Scene.open` never use them. Saving to a `.fbx` path writes Wavefront OBJ text; passing the FBX format object throws; opening an FBX file returns a mesh with no control points and raises no error.

## Environment

- Revision `66cb26df3b031f0bf6976d4e88dc89721983afa4` (default branch `master`)
- Node.js v22.23.3 and npm 10.9.9 (Docker image `node:22-slim`, Linux)
- `npm install` and `npm run build` complete without errors; verified on 2026-10-16

## Steps to reproduce

```sh
npm install
npm run build
node repro.js   # repro.js holds the script below, saved in the repository root
```

```js
const fs = require('fs');
const { Scene } = require('./dist/aspose/threed');
const { Mesh } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/entities');
const { Vector4 } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/utilities');

function triangle() {
  const mesh = new Mesh('tri');
  mesh.controlPoints = [new Vector4(10, 20, 30, 1), new Vector4(11, 20, 30, 1), new Vector4(10, 21, 30, 1)];
  mesh.createPolygon(0, 1, 2);
  return mesh;
}

const { FbxFormat, FbxExporter, FbxSaveOptions } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/formats/fbx');

const scene = new Scene();
scene.rootNode.entity = triangle();

// 1. Save by file extension
scene.save('out.fbx');
console.log(fs.readFileSync('out.fbx', 'utf8').split('\n').slice(0, 3));

// 2. Save with the FBX format object
try { scene.save('out2.fbx', FbxFormat.getInstance()); } catch (e) { console.log(e.message); }

// 3. Open an FBX file (written here with the library's own FbxExporter)
let text = '';
new FbxExporter().export(scene, { write(d) { text += d; } }, new FbxSaveOptions());
fs.writeFileSync('real.fbx', text);
const loaded = new Scene();
loaded.open('real.fbx');
const mesh = loaded.rootNode.childNodes[0].entity;
console.log(mesh.constructor.name, 'control points:', mesh.controlPoints.length);
```

## Expected

1. `out.fbx` contains FBX text (the output of `FbxExporter`).
2. `scene.save('out2.fbx', FbxFormat.getInstance())` saves the file.
3. `loaded.rootNode.childNodes[0].entity` is a mesh with 3 control points.

## Actual result

```
[ '', 'o Node_0', 'v 10.000000 20.000000 30.000000' ]
Unsupported format: FbxFormat
Mesh control points: 0
```
With the geometry on a child node (`createChildNode`), step 1 writes no file at all, because the OBJ exporter that handles the fallback skips child nodes.

## Where in the repository

- `src/aspose/threed/Scene.ts:226-318`: `save` maps the extensions `obj`, `stl`, `gltf`, `glb`, `dae` and `3mf` to a format; there is no `fbx` branch, and `:312-316` falls back to the OBJ format
- `src/aspose/threed/Scene.ts:348-361`: the exporter is chosen from five format names; `FbxFormat` reaches `throw new Error("Unsupported format: ...")` at `:360`
- `src/aspose/threed/Scene.ts:145-223`: `openFromBuffer` detects glTF, 3MF, COLLADA and OBJ and otherwise uses `StlImporter` (`:221`); there is no FBX branch
- `src/aspose/threed/formats/fbx/FbxExporter.ts`, `src/aspose/threed/formats/fbx/FbxImporter.ts`

